    mem:rationale "Same contract gap as the contact-find-by-name finding: typed only wiki:Affordance, escapes wiki:AffordanceDescriptorShape (which targets prof:ResourceDescriptor), so prof:hasRole / rdfs:label / dct:conformsTo / wiki:installedBy are absent. Resolved against /vault/ontology/wiki + /vault/ontology/wikirole. Add the PROF type + four contract predicates; preserve the existing sh:agentInstruction + wiki:selectQuery. SELECT read affordance (solid-pod invoke), NOT an ?ext= surface — no SearchAffordance/dispatch predicates." ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:17:06Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

# --- PROPOSED CORRECTED DESCRIPTOR ------------------------------------------
</vault/meta/affordances/contact-find-by-email.ttl>
    a wiki:Affordance , prof:ResourceDescriptor ;
    prof:hasRole wikirole:affordance ;
    rdfs:label "Contact Find by Email" ;
    dct:conformsTo <http://www.w3.org/TR/dx-prof/> ;
    wiki:installedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/overlay#addressbook> ;
    sh:agentInstruction """
      Email-based contact lookup. Useful when processing inbound messages: given
      the sender's email address, find the corresponding Person card in the
      AddressBook to retrieve identity metadata, affiliations, and wiki links.

      Parameter: $email — the email IRI in mailto: form, e.g.,
      <mailto:user@example.org>. Must be passed as an IRI, not a plain string.

      Sources: </vault/contacts/people.ttl> (aggregated index) plus individual
      Person card files at /vault/contacts/Person/*/index.ttl. Start with the
      aggregated index; fall back to per-card traversal if not found.

      Returns 0..1 ?person IRIs. Multiple results indicate duplicate cards for
      the same email address — surface this to the user as a data quality issue.
    """ ;
    wiki:selectQuery """
PREFIX vcard: <http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#>

SELECT ?person WHERE {
  ?person vcard:hasEmail $email .
}
    """ .

